It is associated with the time of year, as I look forward to facing my 
annual carpet-calling for all the things that I haven't done, and I face 
the members of LLG again telling me that I shouldn't work on any of the fun 
projects because they are lower priority than all the other stuff that 
needs to get done.

At the moment, Nick is unhappy with me for some things I haven't done for 
his project (things that the membership last year said I shouldn't do - I 
was banned from working on the package 0 effort), some book orderers are 
unhappy because their books haven't arrived or because they have bad pages 
that I haven't replaced, and I was recently reminded about the dictionary 
and textbook that I promised would be out in a "couple of months" back in 
1989.  Meanwhile JL and LK have not come out in over 7 years.

I know I've done a lot, but I also know that I've let a lot of people down.

